---------------------------------------------- MODULE ConsolidationTrace -----------------------------------------------
\* Generated by `engramctl formal trace-to-tla` from a schema-v1 log of 4 events of Consolidation. Do not edit.
\* TraceSpec replays the events one per step through the operators of the specification (in a log that records states:
\* through Next, each step pinned to its logged state); the invariants of the configuration are checked on every state
\* of every replay. TraceNotDone is violated exactly when some execution has consumed the whole log, i.e. when the log
\* is a behaviour of the specification.
EXTENDS Consolidation, Naturals, Sequences, TLC

CONSTANTS o2

VARIABLE l

TraceEvents == <<
  [act |-> "ProposeOk", par |-> <<{1, 2, 3, 4}, <<[kind |-> "create", o |-> o2]>>>>],
  [act |-> "ApplyEffectOnly", par |-> <<{1, 2, 3, 4}>>],
  [act |-> "Crash", par |-> << >>],
  [act |-> "ApplyEffectOnly", par |-> <<{1, 2, 3, 4}>>]
>>

tvars == <<vars, l>>

TraceInit == Init /\ l = 1

TraceReplay ==
  /\ l <= Len(TraceEvents)
  /\ l' = l + 1
  /\ \/ FALSE
     \/ TraceEvents[l].act = "ProposeOk" /\ ProposeOk(TraceEvents[l].par[1], TraceEvents[l].par[2])
     \/ TraceEvents[l].act = "ApplyEffectOnly" /\ ApplyEffectOnly(TraceEvents[l].par[1])
     \/ TraceEvents[l].act = "Crash" /\ Crash

\* One step after the last event, so that every state of the replay is checked against the invariants before
\* TraceNotDone can fail (TLC checks a state when it generates it).
TraceFinish == l = Len(TraceEvents) + 1 /\ l' = l + 1 /\ UNCHANGED vars

TraceNext == TraceReplay \/ TraceFinish

TraceSpec == TraceInit /\ [][TraceNext]_tvars

TraceNotDone == l <= Len(TraceEvents) + 1

========================================================================================================================
